From 845b21f013758dbbe4dcc957c2a831eb275ff535 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:26:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] feat(core): trim structured list rows; say when a list
 is empty (C22, C15)

The structured rows of resources_list and the pod lists repeated what
the request already fixes (apiVersion and kind on every row, Namespace
when a namespace was given) and carried every column kubectl prints
only with -o wide (Pods: IP, Node, Nominated Node, Readiness Gates;
Deployments: Containers, Images, Selector). On the native session that
was 6,538 tokens of structured rows the agent did not use; Claude Code
shows the model only the structured channel.

- Structured rows drop apiVersion and kind, Namespace when a namespace
  was given, and every column the API marks priority > 0 (the -o wide
  columns). A new `wide: true` argument keeps the wide columns.
- An empty result says so: "# No <Kind> found in namespace <ns>
  matching labelSelector ..." instead of an empty text, which agents
  read as ambiguous (28 calls on the native session). The structured
  content of an empty table list stays absent, as before.
- The text table (C11, held) is unchanged, and nothing changes when MCP
  Apps are enabled, whose UI renders the full rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
